>>  This file will be updated as Faqs are asked and answered  <<
Last update : Tabitha Feb 15 95

Currently we have no Frequently Asked Questions, but i can see a few
that we might get, so lets nip them in the bud and answer them.  :)

**  What if i hate the way you have joined my cabal to Eternal City ?

Please note that the methods of joining cabals to EC as suggested
in the Connections file are just that, suggestions.  We will *not* connect a
cabal without the approval of its leader/s.  Please talk to us about your  
cabal's needs.  We will happily re-arrange things to try and satisfy everyone.
If an agreement really cannot be reached, prehaps the possibility of the
cabal entry being off another cabal, instead of eternal, should be considered.


**  How much work will these changes make for cabal leaders ?

As little as possible.  :)  For many cabals, nothing additional will be
required.  For some, however, especially those connected by the wharf or the
transit port, an few rooms may need to be created or altered within the cabal.
If you do not wish to do this coding yourself, we will create or alter the
relevent rooms in our own directories and present them to you for your approval
and implication onto the mud.
    -Nothing will be put into your cabal directory without your approval.-


**  How much will the Eternal City itself change?  

>> ( Eternal Cabal Page, Rookie wrote: )
>> My only bitch ( if you can call it that ) is that EC does have some
>> nostaligia associated with it, and to change it to drastically can
>> lose that.

The basic layout and descriptions of EC will remain.  We would not think
so highly of ourselves as to mess with tradition.  :)  The only direct change
to the City that we have planned is the removal of the linear cabal exits
and trans objects.  The bulk of our project is concerned with EC's
surrounds.
